message: "If you use this exercise, its code or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ICESat-2 and GEDI against airborne lidar at Québec's permanent forest plots: a reproducible exercise"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-11
authors:
  - family-names: Czarnecki de Liz
    given-names: João Paulo
    affiliation: Université Laval
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1860-346X"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/joaoczarnecki/ICESAT_GEDI_ALS_FRI_QUEBEC_Exercise"
url: "https://joaoczarnecki.github.io/ICESAT_GEDI_ALS_FRI_QUEBEC_Exercise/"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, step-by-step exercise comparing spaceborne lidar canopy heights (ICESat-2 ATL08 and GEDI L2A,
  obtained through SlideRule Earth) with airborne lidar (ALS) at about 10,000 permanent sample plots of Québec.
  It covers the masked download of satellite samples near the plots, pairing with forest disturbance records,
  agreement at the plot and with distance, the cost of the delay between acquisitions, forest type and ALS season,
  and, in one region, a footprint-by-footprint comparison with ALS on the same ground. Code in R and Python (MIT),
  text and figures CC BY 4.0. Developed with Claude (Anthropic) as an AI coding assistant.
keywords:
